[{"id":"VRCE-3-45-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":1,"english":"Being thus addressed by Rāvaņa under the guise of a mendicant, desirous of carrying her away Vaidehī thought within herself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"863f2263c7c4ae92c48b8b83f5815b56a8f3084829498592b83d203a0217d972","compact":"110d13355185960dfe0625c4ad3be990fa3c6214cac3422e37cc8b54d2bbd3a1","nasal":"110d13355185960dfe0625c4ad3be990fa3c6214cac3422e37cc8b54d2bbd3a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":2,"english":"This person is my guest and a Brahmin; he may curse me if I do not speak to him. Thinking this for a moment Sītā said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f00219ae0f4b8551b72554f0a0bdec92ee680d2924fef783c2a80f80f2f1b051","compact":"c9177bbdcf8d2edf5d862636fa1fd45e289120271c9e597a968705f4d4149215","nasal":"c9177bbdcf8d2edf5d862636fa1fd45e289120271c9e597a968705f4d4149215"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":3,"english":"May good betide you! I am the daughter of the high-souled Janaka, the king of Mithilā, the beloved Queen of Rāma and my name is Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fde077df888cef8e81200d6d964467855166f010791d9c3dca3b65d1924eb326","compact":"4246c5e9982d5a884884545f05cd873675f7f5ed2bf8744451aa366ce89e6c67","nasal":"4246c5e9982d5a884884545f05cd873675f7f5ed2bf8744451aa366ce89e6c67"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":4,"english":"Dwelling in the palace of Ikşäkus for twelve years, I enjoyed many things passing human and had all my desires satisfied.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.603,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74ebe62c2effff5151bb2f0accab0e65332f8749f7736abde6299fd7b4e271f2","compact":"32b169ebe40da5a7a544931bfc9ddf8660bffc1cc523c7185af24b98c70facb4","nasal":"59f4541d6487cbae23f8e78ddfe46c1f3e14fc822bb7db23a35af6d316e78d44"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":5,"english":"On the thirteenth year king (Dasaratha) counselled with his ministers about the installation of Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.441,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"18e9d00e01cbc2a5ebdf828e3cd0dcd043749f4ee1e76a768ad9b05fb8f36a9d","compact":"32203d7fab8c79acae609d454a15f4f1cc6310cf7dec2aed9ba7d1777ff2cfe1","nasal":"1fce88adeb3ecbf872a2060fdc655ce545e07ae53208f33ba1adf784ddca8682"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":6,"english":"Accordingly everything necessary for the installation being made ready, KaikeyI, one of my mothers-in-law, begged of her husband a boon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"14dad59de339fea84913c66fcb0dd4bbb27e6426e212038aca241f2e49a19d45","compact":"167127f2eb6bec218b697a0c9dc9539c0f3678dfdfef29b8551c8b47334ae6e4","nasal":"167127f2eb6bec218b697a0c9dc9539c0f3678dfdfef29b8551c8b47334ae6e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":7,"english":"Bringing my father-in-law under control by means of her virtuous deeds, Kaikeyi begged, of that truthful, best of monarchs, two boons namely the exile of my husband into woods and the installation of Bharata,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a2e9d5fb8cf48bbb4d2cb57af4f0a70c7c3578726c78e6b4fbe0c64bf08e7301","compact":"e1b8c6452100bc4eb2c0728dbe83b0e4ea39fdddd2a420256370abf87d4cfb92","nasal":"e1b8c6452100bc4eb2c0728dbe83b0e4ea39fdddd2a420256370abf87d4cfb92"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":8,"english":"And said-I shall never eat, drink or sleep and (if Rāma be installed) I shall end my life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c6ce07f091a7b13a7bf6a605a4fd4564a8d400d4d94e6b9b1596cd1bf72494b","compact":"1c9bafaa4f2ddc5511a545d31cc033fd0dcc7026d3fd172392deea7249d149f6","nasal":"7d5e99ae8f07c87103b3f2be62593c55a5731301f8e2d745516c60a5d0498e66"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":9,"english":"Kaikeyī speaking thus, that lord of earth, my father-in-law begged her to accept diverse riches; but Kaikeyi did not agree.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.516,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b40ab6a7b07375b14ed4b67cc4a51321dd3304f269e8c835957c51e22a190a5","compact":"66e33c359511c11151c82a247118095f90cbcf089d1ecc4589d86901c8678e3d","nasal":"66e33c359511c11151c82a247118095f90cbcf089d1ecc4589d86901c8678e3d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":10,"english":"My husband is known all over the world under the name of Rāma he is truthful, goodnatured, of pure character, ever engaged in the welfare of all created beings, of mighty-arms and expansive eyes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.456,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4cf37b4070e09d221fcaf76ed82e68b06b20171d5f911cc71832b2783849a234","compact":"e6bff1c5e21a6e2f8eb4859aa8cba6754dcbe57be7d669ae8a0e59fb6cc6f162","nasal":"257a1b0d37894660ef019296ea27c1e095bbb5d3180a55252edab17bf9b8bf46"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":11,"english":"When Rāma came to his father for being installed Kaikeyi spoke to my husband the following cruel words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f17985ec573c949d85c43167390c99cb58ae4abfff882007abec4b196eeb5823","compact":"4a97a9c462e25af2ab9fec6e421064d66e47feb14f3d89e3cdd2d846567ce324","nasal":"4a97a9c462e25af2ab9fec6e421064d66e47feb14f3d89e3cdd2d846567ce324"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":12,"english":"Do you hear, O Rāghava, how I have been ordered by your Sire. This kingdom, rid of thorns is to be conferred of Bharata, and you shall have to sojourn into woods for years nine and five. Do you therefore repair to forest, O Kākutstha and save your Sire from untruth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2f4cce8df0047804db0f087b4d42d0ef399669503017547f19dd036c3cf51c8","compact":"4fe2053c2156115297615bc0dae453863f0895cb65af641eccbb2415b8bdf059","nasal":"1b6fa7acff8493e22a9a19f421817099d43d318310a723c5483e5a12719fcc1a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":13,"english":"Do you hear, O Rāghava, how I have been ordered by your Sire. This kingdom, rid of thorns is to be conferred of Bharata, and you shall have to sojourn into woods for years nine and five. Do you therefore repair to forest, O Kākutstha and save your Sire from untruth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e1f2f1d53c93a557dbb5d0073004cc7727aae708cdf93879c1b984d97840af5","compact":"da9fdc7c2654dc5cc3b497e40f50cdf31ad95ea2a28d5e59dd214985f21ef237","nasal":"18428bc059dc487be0f10cf64d807d192329d4411098918e1a83255f35a32cd1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":14,"english":"Whereto Rāma fearlessly replied 'So be it!' Hearing her words my husband of firm vows acted accordingly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.618,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"81cb7dc1f1ba4872367d23c884f2cea0da68d0d400681d19c038e83dbde963aa","compact":"51d028731175705ee06f989a62060d1b93d83427521050907873701ecededaa2","nasal":"51d028731175705ee06f989a62060d1b93d83427521050907873701ecededaa2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":15,"english":"He always maketh gifts and taketh none. He always speaketh truth and never telleth an untruth. This is his best observance O Brāhmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.753,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3785afaac0683d5292e16a7f91eff84885eb30aa83480b52f92abc26bef6079b","compact":"2692ed8ddbfd61f999ac3b2b67fd9702088b9a7f62fe15c7d13fc81336c3f42b","nasal":"f05df6225967a4169778ef715bcc3e244d72c437717b1015a399f500c41ea54b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":16,"english":"His half-brother named Lakşmaņa is of mighty prowess. That best of men is Rāma's help and the destroyer of foes in battle. That brother of his named Lakşmaņa is of firm resolution and given to asceticism.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c9b1b419374d6838ecb5b2a429498843235f1562332f01ed4630ce75f1b6fe0c","compact":"234dd674f32f2858cd3d7c6ab30c6928f64721463d87c7b458b54929d0824abf","nasal":"234dd674f32f2858cd3d7c6ab30c6928f64721463d87c7b458b54929d0824abf"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":17,"english":"His half-brother named Lakşmaņa is of mighty prowess. That best of men is Rāma's help and the destroyer of foes in battle. That brother of his named Lakşmaņa is of firm resolution and given to asceticism. With a bow in hand he has followed (Rama) flying as an exile to woods along with me. Thus that one (Rāma) of firm resolution and ever engaged in pious offices wearing matted hair and assuming the semblance of an ascetic has entered this forest of Dandaka along with myself and his younger brother,","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.476,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-17","DUTT-3-47-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"676653d662ad18e7a5a7b69e27764b625ee48ba64614eb7b4001b9a676f9c195","compact":"da19bb605b9f9413a3daa67c37b49f3bad944cfe2c0cf041f0a993013c5f7a01","nasal":"85b8cf7a0e246b13f162132a61b7079350b1e2f2e7710fb31c95ef679dd196c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":18,"english":"O you the best of twice-born ones, we three being deprived of our kingdom by Kaikeyi have been living in this dense forest by virtue of our ! effulgence. Do you take heart for a moment and live here. Instantly shall my husband return with good many wild fruits and roots and with sufficient meat after killing many a deer, hog and Gosamp. Truly do you relate to me your name, Gotra and leneage. O you twice-born one, why do you range alone in this forest of Dandaka?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"370e4d0a346bae4765a01f89c9d8f5e3bc1ddbb9dfea2a988cd0606669bb5191","compact":"6a920ffe883b0ddfbdd462e4961ae3222505ca94065f2da98b780400a8be80b7","nasal":"8b2eb81675b50336051856289b0214a9275b1f54f6996fa45c095771eefb36e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":19,"english":"O you the best of twice-born ones, we three being deprived of our kingdom by Kaikeyi have been living in this dense forest by virtue of our ! effulgence. Do you take heart for a moment and live here. Instantly shall my husband return with good many wild fruits and roots and with sufficient meat after killing many a deer, hog and Gosamp. Truly do you relate to me your name, Gotra and leneage. O you twice-born one, why do you range alone in this forest of Dandaka?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c92f73ba06b3a395d5a97030c3b077388982c28fd905f1cf41494501e31b981","compact":"77f2d3105847b9bcd748b2be057ad17230d8b2f7dd9fb114f93426f36224119e","nasal":"77f2d3105847b9bcd748b2be057ad17230d8b2f7dd9fb114f93426f36224119e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":20,"english":"O you the best of twice-born ones, we three being deprived of our kingdom by Kaikeyi have been living in this dense forest by virtue of our ! effulgence. Do you take heart for a moment and live here. Instantly shall my husband return with good many wild fruits and roots and with sufficient meat after killing many a deer, hog and Gosamp. Truly do you relate to me your name, Gotra and leneage. O you twice-born one, why do you range alone in this forest of Dandaka?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-47-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3045020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b65c5fce24fca254a57bf7a0fa7db996ac0d50f1b831b6bbc7b2959dee37353f","compact":"b797d0e09b96dfd94114269315a89ef401f1430f732165ec5377536def7f9331","nasal":"64562c448e5f7b18bc6ae49bc3438aee898b7efb6e61babe54cf0b1fa941da6f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-45-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":45,"verse":21,"english":"Sītā the wife of Rāma speaking thus, the mighty Lord of Rākşasas-Rävana replied with these harsh words,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.735,"